  "id": "COMPOUND:18274 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between ent-Intermedeol and Raji cells, mediated through the SNU-387 target. Multiple paths indicate that ent-Intermedeol interacts with SNU-387, which is a target of several compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. These compounds all have a common target of Raji cells, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible link between ent-Intermedeol and Raji, likely through the inhibition of a common target molecule. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where ent-Intermedeol may act by targeting SNU-387, which in turn affects Raji cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for ent-Intermedeol in modulating Raji cell activity through the SNU-387 target.",
